msgid "FAQ: The admin"
msgstr "Ceisteanna Coitianta: An admin"

msgid ""
"I can't log in. When I enter a valid username and password, it just brings "
"up the login page again, with no error messages."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir liom logáil isteach. Nuair a chuirim ainm úsáideora agus pasfhocal "
"bailí isteach, ní thugann sé ach an leathanach logála isteach arís, gan aon "
"teachtaireachtaí earráide."

msgid ""
"The login cookie isn't being set correctly, because the domain of the cookie "
"sent out by Django doesn't match the domain in your browser. Try setting "
"the :setting:`SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN` setting to match your domain. For "
"example, if you're going to \"https://www.example.com/admin/\" in your "
"browser, set ``SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN = 'www.example.com'``."
msgstr ""
"Níl an fianán logála isteach á shocrú i gceart, toisc nach bhfuil fearann an "
"fhianáin a sheol Django amach comhoiriúnach leis an bhfearann i do "
"bhrabhsálaí. Bain triail as an socrú :setting:'SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN' a "
"shocrú chun d'fhearann a mheaitseáil. Mar shampla, má tá tú chun \"https://"
"www.example.com/admin/\" a dhéanamh i do bhrabhsálaí, socraigh "
"''SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN = 'www.example.com'''."

msgid ""
"I can't log in. When I enter a valid username and password, it brings up the "
"login page again, with a \"Please enter a correct username and password\" "
"error."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir liom logáil isteach. Nuair a chuirim ainm úsáideora agus pasfhocal "
"bailí isteach, tugann sé suas an leathanach logála isteach arís, le earráid "
"\"Cuir isteach ainm úsáideora agus pasfhocal ceart\"."

msgid ""
"If you're sure your username and password are correct, make sure your user "
"account has :attr:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.is_active` "
"and :attr:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.is_staff` set to True. The admin "
"site only allows access to users with those two fields both set to True."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú cinnte go bhfuil d'ainm úsáideora agus do phasfhocal ceart, déan "
"cinnte go bhfuil :attr:'~django.contrib.auth.models.User.is_active' "
"agus :attr:'~django.contrib.auth.models.User.is_staff' leagtha ar True. Ní "
"cheadaíonn an suíomh riaracháin ach rochtain ar úsáideoirí leis an dá réimse "
"sin atá leagtha síos go Fíor."

msgid ""
"How do I automatically set a field's value to the user who last edited the "
"object in the admin?"
msgstr ""
"Conas is féidir liom luach réimse a shocrú go huathoibríoch don úsáideoir a "
"rinne eagarthóireacht dheireanach ar an réad sa admin?"

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin` class provides customization "
"hooks that allow you to transform an object as it saved, using details from "
"the request. By extracting the current user from the request, and "
"customizing the :meth:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.save_model` hook, "
"you can update an object to reflect the user that edited it. See :ref:`the "
"documentation on ModelAdmin methods <model-admin-methods>` for an example."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an rang :'~ django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin' crúcaí "
"saincheaptha a ligeann duit rud a athrú mar a shábháil sé, ag baint úsáide "
"as sonraí ón iarratas. Tríd an úsáideoir reatha a bhaint as an iarratas, "
"agus an hook :meth:'~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.save_model' a "
"shaincheapadh, is féidir leat réad a nuashonrú chun an t-úsáideoir a chuir "
"in eagar é a léiriú. Féach:ref:'the documentation on ModelAdmin "
"methods<model-admin-methods>' mar shampla."

msgid ""
"How do I limit admin access so that objects can only be edited by the users "
"who created them?"
msgstr ""
"Conas is féidir liom rochtain riaracháin a theorannú ionas nach féidir ach "
"leis na húsáideoirí a chruthaigh iad rudaí a chur in eagar?"

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin` class also provides "
"customization hooks that allow you to control the visibility and editability "
"of objects in the admin. Using the same trick of extracting the user from "
"the request, the :meth:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.get_queryset` "
"and :meth:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.has_change_permission` can be "
"used to control the visibility and editability of objects in the admin."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an rang :'~ django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin' crúcaí "
"saincheaptha a ligeann duit infheictheacht agus ineagarthóireachtacht rudaí "
"sa admin a rialú. Ag baint úsáide as an cleas céanna a bhaint as an "
"úsáideoir as an iarratas, is féidir "
"an :meth:'~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.get_queryset' "
"agus :meth:'~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.has_change_permission' a úsáid "
"chun infheictheacht agus ineagarthóireachtacht rudaí sa admin a rialú."

msgid ""
"My admin-site CSS and images showed up fine using the development server, "
"but they're not displaying when using mod_wsgi."
msgstr ""
"Léirigh mo CSS agus íomhánna admin-site fíneáil ag baint úsáide as an "
"bhfreastalaí forbartha, ach níl siad ag taispeáint nuair a bhíonn mod_wsgi á "
"n-úsáid."

msgid ""
"See :ref:`serving the admin files <serving-the-admin-files>` in the \"How to "
"use Django with mod_wsgi\" documentation."
msgstr ""
"Féach: ref: 'ag freastal ar na comhaid admin<serving-the-admin-files>' sa "
"doiciméadú \"Conas Django a úsáid le mod_wsgi\"."

msgid ""
"My \"list_filter\" contains a ManyToManyField, but the filter doesn't "
"display."
msgstr ""
"Tá ManyToManyField i mo \"list_filter\", ach ní thaispeánann an scagaire."

msgid ""
"Django won't bother displaying the filter for a ``ManyToManyField`` if there "
"are no related objects."
msgstr ""
"Ní bhacfaidh Django leis an scagaire a thaispeáint le haghaidh "
"''ManyToManyField'' mura bhfuil aon rudaí gaolmhara ann."

msgid ""
"For example, if your :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_filter` "
"includes :doc:`sites </ref/contrib/sites>`, and there are no sites in your "
"database, it won't display a \"Site\" filter. In that case, filtering by "
"site would be meaningless."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má chuimsíonn "
"do :attr:'~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_filter' :d oc:'sites </ref/"
"contrib/sites>', agus níl aon suíomhanna i do bhunachar sonraí, ní "
"thaispeánfaidh sé scagaire \"Suíomh\". Sa chás sin, bheadh scagadh de réir "
"suímh gan bhrí."

msgid "Some objects aren't appearing in the admin."
msgstr "Níl roinnt rudaí le feiceáil sa admin."

msgid ""
"Inconsistent row counts may be caused by missing foreign key values or a "
"foreign key field incorrectly set to :attr:`null=False "
"<django.db.models.Field.null>`. If you have a record with "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey` pointing to a nonexistent object and "
"that foreign key is included "
"is :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_display`, the record will "
"not be shown in the admin changelist because the Django model is declaring "
"an integrity constraint that is not implemented at the database level."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh comhaireamh as a chéile neamhréireach a bheith mar thoradh ar "
"eochairluachanna eachtracha ar iarraidh nó réimse eochair eachtrach a "
"leagtar go mícheart chun:attr:'null=False <django.db.models.Field.null>'. Má "
"tá taifead agat le :class:'~django.db.models.ForeignKey' ag díriú ar rud "
"nach bhfuil ann agus go bhfuil eochair eachtrach san áireamh ná: attr: '~ "
"django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_display', ní thaispeánfar an taifead sa "
"changelist admin toisc go bhfuil an tsamhail Django ag dearbhú srian sláine "
"nach gcuirtear i bhfeidhm ag leibhéal an bhunachair sonraí."

msgid "How can I customize the functionality of the admin interface?"
msgstr ""
"Conas is féidir liom feidhmiúlacht an chomhéadain riaracháin a shaincheapadh?"

msgid ""
"You've got several options. If you want to piggyback on top of an add/change "
"form that Django automatically generates, you can attach arbitrary "
"JavaScript modules to the page via the model's class Admin :ref:`js "
"parameter <modeladmin-asset-definitions>`. That parameter is a list of URLs, "
"as strings, pointing to JavaScript modules that will be included within the "
"admin form via a ``<script>`` tag."
msgstr ""
"Tá roinnt roghanna agat. Más mian leat piggyback ar bharr foirm add / athrú "
"a ghineann Django go huathoibríoch, is féidir leat modúil treallach "
"JavaScript a cheangal leis an leathanach trí rang an mhúnla Riarachán: ref: "
"'js parameter <modeladmin-asset-definitions>'. Is liosta URLanna é an "
"paraiméadar sin, mar teaghráin, a dhíríonn ar mhodúil JavaScript a chuirfear "
"san áireamh san fhoirm riaracháin trí chlib ''<script>'''."

msgid ""
"If you want more flexibility than is feasible by tweaking the auto-generated "
"forms, feel free to write custom views for the admin. The admin is powered "
"by Django itself, and you can write custom views that hook into the "
"authentication system, check permissions and do whatever else they need to "
"do."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat níos mó solúbthachta ná mar is indéanta trí tweaking na "
"foirmeacha uathoibríoch-ghintear, bíodh leisce ort tuairimí saincheaptha a "
"scríobh don admin. Tá an admin faoi thiomáint ag Django féin, agus is féidir "
"leat tuairimí saincheaptha a scríobh a théann isteach sa chóras "
"fíordheimhnithe, ceadanna a sheiceáil agus cibé rud eile is gá dóibh a "
"dhéanamh."

msgid ""
"If you want to customize the look-and-feel of the admin interface, read the "
"next question."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat cuma-agus-mothú an chomhéadain riaracháin a shaincheapadh, "
"léigh an chéad cheist eile."

msgid "The dynamically-generated admin site is ugly! How can I change it?"
msgstr ""
"Tá an suíomh riaracháin a ghintear go dinimiciúil gránna! Conas is féidir "
"liom é a athrú?"

msgid ""
"We like it, but if you don't agree, you can modify the admin site's "
"presentation by editing the CSS stylesheet and/or associated image files. "
"The site is built using semantic HTML and plenty of CSS hooks, so any "
"changes you'd like to make should be possible by editing the stylesheet."
msgstr ""
"Is maith linn é, ach mura n-aontaíonn tú, is féidir leat cur i láthair an "
"tsuímh riaracháin a mhodhnú trí eagarthóireacht a dhéanamh ar stílbhileog "
"CSS agus / nó comhaid íomhá ghaolmhara. Tá an suíomh tógtha ag baint úsáide "
"as HTML séimeantach agus neart crúcaí CSS, mar sin ba chóir go mbeadh aon "
"athruithe ar mhaith leat a dhéanamh indéanta tríd an stílbhileog a chur in "
"eagar."

msgid "What browsers are supported for using the admin?"
msgstr "Cad iad na brabhsálaithe a dtacaítear leo chun an riarthóir a úsáid?"

msgid ""
"The admin provides a fully-functional experience to the recent versions of "
"modern, web standards compliant browsers. On desktop this means Chrome, "
"Edge, Firefox, Opera, Safari, and others."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an admin taithí lánfheidhmiúil do na leaganacha le déanaí de "
"bhrabhsálaithe nua-aimseartha, caighdeáin ghréasáin comhlíontacha. Ar an "
"deasc ciallaíonn sé seo Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Opera, Safari, agus daoine "
"eile."

msgid ""
"On mobile and tablet devices, the admin provides a responsive experience for "
"web standards compliant browsers. This includes the major browsers on both "
"Android and iOS."
msgstr ""
"Ar ghléasanna soghluaiste agus táibléid, soláthraíonn an riarachán taithí "
"fhreagrach do bhrabhsálaithe comhlíontacha caighdeáin ghréasáin. Áirítear "
"leis seo na brabhsálaithe móra ar Android agus iOS araon."

msgid ""
"Depending on feature support, there *may* be minor stylistic differences "
"between browsers. These are considered acceptable variations in rendering."
msgstr ""
"Ag brath ar thacaíocht gné, d'fhéadfadh *a bheith * miondifríochtaí stíle "
"idir brabhsálaithe. Meastar gur éagsúlachtaí inghlactha iad seo sa rindreáil."

msgid "What assistive technologies are supported for using the admin?"
msgstr ""
"Cad iad na teicneolaíochtaí cúnta a dtacaítear leo chun an riarachán a úsáid?"

msgid ""
"The admin is intended to be compatible with a wide range of assistive "
"technologies, but there are currently many blockers. The support target is "
"all latest versions of major assistive technologies, including Dragon, JAWS, "
"NVDA, Orca, TalkBack, Voice Control, VoiceOver iOS, VoiceOver macOS, Windows "
"Contrast Themes, ZoomText, and screen magnifiers."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé i gceist go mbeadh an riarachán comhoiriúnach le raon leathan "
"teicneolaíochtaí cúnta, ach tá go leor bacadóirí ann faoi láthair. Is é an "
"sprioc tacaíochta na leaganacha is déanaí de theicneolaíochtaí cúnta móra, "
"lena n-áirítear Dragon, JAWS, NVDA, Orca, TalkBack, Rialú Gutha, iOS "
"VoiceOver, macOS VoiceOver, Téamaí Codarsnachta Windows, ZoomText, agus "
"formhéadaitheoirí scáileáin."

msgid "FAQ: Contributing code"
msgstr "Ceisteanna Coitianta: Cód a chur leis"

msgid "How can I get started contributing code to Django?"
msgstr "Conas is féidir liom tús a chur le cód a chur le Django?"

msgid ""
"Thanks for asking! We've written an entire document devoted to this "
"question. It's titled :doc:`Contributing to Django </internals/contributing/"
"index>`."
msgstr ""
"Go raibh maith agat as a iarraidh! Tá cáipéis iomlán scríofa againn atá "
"dírithe ar an gceist seo. Is é an teideal atá air ná :d oc:'Contributing to "
"Django </internals/contributing/index>'."

msgid ""
"I submitted a bug fix several weeks ago. Why are you ignoring my "
"contribution?"
msgstr ""
"Chuir mé fabht isteach roinnt seachtainí ó shin. Cén fáth a bhfuil neamhaird "
"á déanamh agat ar mo ranníocaíocht?"

msgid "Don't worry: We're not ignoring you!"
msgstr "Ná bíodh imní ort: Nílimid ag déanamh neamhaird ort!"

msgid ""
"It's important to understand there is a difference between \"a ticket is "
"being ignored\" and \"a ticket has not been attended to yet.\" Django's "
"ticket system contains hundreds of open tickets, of various degrees of "
"impact on end-user functionality, and Django's developers have to review and "
"prioritize."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé tábhachtach a thuiscint go bhfuil difríocht idir \"tá neamhaird á "
"déanamh ar thicéad\" agus \"níor freastalaíodh ar thicéad go fóill.\" Tá na "
"céadta ticéad oscailte i gcóras ticéad Django, de chéimeanna éagsúla "
"tionchair ar fheidhmiúlacht úsáideora deiridh, agus caithfidh forbróirí "
"Django athbhreithniú agus tosaíocht a thabhairt."

msgid ""
"On top of that: the people who work on Django are all volunteers. As a "
"result, the amount of time that we have to work on the framework is limited "
"and will vary from week to week depending on our spare time. If we're busy, "
"we may not be able to spend as much time on Django as we might want."
msgstr ""
"Anuas air sin: is oibrithe deonacha iad na daoine a oibríonn ar Django. Mar "
"thoradh air sin, tá teorainn leis an méid ama a chaithfimid a bheith ag "
"obair ar an gcreatlach agus beidh sé éagsúil ó sheachtain go seachtain ag "
"brath ar ár n-am saor. Má tá muid gnóthach, b'fhéidir nach mbeimid in ann an "
"oiread ama a chaitheamh ar Django agus a bheadh uainn."

msgid ""
"The best way to make sure tickets do not get hung up on the way to checkin "
"is to make it dead easy, even for someone who may not be intimately familiar "
"with that area of the code, to understand the problem and verify the fix:"
msgstr ""
"Is é an bealach is fearr chun a chinntiú nach bhfuil ticéid a fháil crochadh "
"suas ar an mbealach chun checkin é a dhéanamh marbh éasca, fiú do dhuine "
"nach féidir a bheith eolach go pearsanta leis an réimse sin den chód, chun "
"tuiscint a fháil ar an bhfadhb agus a fhíorú an shocrú:"

msgid ""
"Are there clear instructions on how to reproduce the bug? If this touches a "
"dependency (such as Pillow), a contrib module, or a specific database, are "
"those instructions clear enough even for someone not familiar with it?"
msgstr ""
"An bhfuil treoracha soiléire ann maidir le conas an fabht a atáirgeadh? Má "
"bhaineann sé seo le spleáchas (mar shampla Pillow), modúl contrib, nó "
"bunachar sonraí ar leith, an bhfuil na treoracha sin soiléir go leor fiú do "
"dhuine nach bhfuil eolach air?"

msgid ""
"If there are several branches linked to the ticket, is it clear what each "
"one does, which ones can be ignored and which matter?"
msgstr ""
"Má tá roinnt brainsí nasctha leis an ticéad, an bhfuil sé soiléir cad a "
"dhéanann gach ceann, cé na cinn is féidir neamhaird a dhéanamh orthu agus "
"cén t-ábhar?"

msgid ""
"Does the change include a unit test? If not, is there a very clear "
"explanation why not? A test expresses succinctly what the problem is, and "
"shows that the branch actually fixes it."
msgstr ""
"An bhfuil tástáil aonaid san áireamh san athrú? Mura bhfuil, an bhfuil míniú "
"an-soiléir ann cén fáth nach bhfuil? Cuireann tástáil in iúl go gonta cad é "
"an fhadhb, agus taispeánann sé go socraíonn an brainse é i ndáiríre."

msgid ""
"If your contribution is not suitable for inclusion in Django, we won't "
"ignore it -- we'll close the ticket. So if your ticket is still open, it "
"doesn't mean we're ignoring you; it just means we haven't had time to look "
"at it yet."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil do ranníocaíocht oiriúnach le cur san áireamh in Django, ní "
"dhéanfaimid neamhaird air -- dúnfaimid an ticéad. Mar sin, má tá do thicéad "
"fós ar oscailt, ní chiallaíonn sé go bhfuil neamhaird á déanamh againn ort; "
"ciallaíonn sé nach raibh am againn breathnú air go fóill."

msgid "When and how might I remind the team of a change I care about?"
msgstr ""
"Cathain agus conas a d'fhéadfainn athrú a bhfuil cúram orm a chur i gcuimhne "
"don fhoireann?"

msgid ""
"A polite, well-timed message in the forum/branch is one way to get "
"attention. To determine the right time, you need to keep an eye on the "
"schedule. If you post your message right before a release deadline, you're "
"not likely to get the sort of attention you require."
msgstr ""
"Bealach amháin chun aird a fháil is ea teachtaireacht bhéasach, dhea-"
"thráthúil san fhóram/sa chraobh. Chun an t-am ceart a chinneadh, ní mór duit "
"súil a choinneáil ar an sceideal. Má chuireann tú do theachtaireacht sa "
"phost díreach roimh spriocdháta scaoilte, ní dócha go bhfaighidh tú an "
"cineál aire a theastaíonn uait."

msgid ""
"Gentle reminders in the ``#contributing-getting-started`` channel in the "
"`Django Discord server`_ can work."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Another way to get traction is to pull several related tickets together. "
"When someone sits down to review a bug in an area they haven't touched for a "
"while, it can take a few minutes to remember all the fine details of how "
"that area of code works. If you collect several minor bug fixes together "
"into a similarly themed group, you make an attractive target, as the cost of "
"coming up to speed on an area of code can be spread over multiple tickets."
msgstr ""
"Bealach eile chun tarraingt a fháil ná roinnt ticéad gaolmhar a tharraingt "
"le chéile. Nuair a shuíonn duine síos chun athbhreithniú a dhéanamh ar "
"fhabht i gceantar nach bhfuil siad i dteagmháil léi ar feadh tamaill, is "
"féidir é a ghlacadh cúpla nóiméad chun cuimhneamh ar na sonraí fíneáil ar "
"conas a oibríonn an réimse sin de chód. Má bhailíonn tú roinnt ceartúcháin "
"mionfhabht le chéile i ngrúpa téamaí den chineál céanna, déanann tú sprioc "
"tharraingteach, mar is féidir an costas a bhaineann le teacht suas le luas "
"ar réimse cód a scaipeadh thar thicéid éagsúla."

msgid ""
"Please refrain from emailing anyone personally or repeatedly raising the "
"same issue over and over again. This sort of behavior will not gain you any "
"additional attention -- certainly not the attention that you need in order "
"to get your issue addressed."
msgstr ""
"Ná seol ríomhphost chuig duine ar bith go pearsanta nó arís agus arís eile "
"ag ardú na ceiste céanna arís agus arís eile. Ní bhfaighidh an cineál "
"iompair seo aon aird bhreise duit - is cinnte nach bhfuil an aird a "
"theastaíonn uait chun aghaidh a thabhairt ar do cheist."

msgid ""
"But I've reminded you several times and you keep ignoring my contribution!"
msgstr ""
"Ach chuir mé i gcuimhne duit arís agus arís eile agus coinníonn tú neamhaird "
"ar mo ranníocaíocht!"

msgid ""
"Seriously - we're not ignoring you. If your contribution is not suitable for "
"inclusion in Django, we will close the ticket. For all the other tickets, we "
"need to prioritize our efforts, which means that some tickets will be "
"addressed before others."
msgstr ""
"Dáiríre - níl muid ag déanamh neamhaird ort. Mura bhfuil do ranníocaíocht "
"oiriúnach le cur san áireamh in Django, dúnfaimid an ticéad. I gcás na "
"dticéad eile go léir, ní mór dúinn tús áite a thabhairt dár n-iarrachtaí, "
"rud a chiallaíonn go dtabharfar aghaidh ar roinnt ticéad os comhair daoine "
"eile."

msgid ""
"One of the criteria that is used to prioritize bug fixes is the number of "
"people that will likely be affected by a given bug. Bugs that have the "
"potential to affect many people will generally get priority over those that "
"are edge cases."
msgstr ""
"Ceann de na critéir a úsáidtear chun tús áite a thabhairt do shocrú "
"fabhtanna ná líon na ndaoine ar dócha go mbeidh tionchar ag fabht ar leith "
"orthu. Is iondúil go dtabharfar tús áite do fhabhtanna a d'fhéadfadh dul i "
"bhfeidhm ar go leor daoine orthu siúd ar cásanna imeallacha iad."

msgid ""
"Another reason that a bug might be ignored for a while is if the bug is a "
"symptom of a larger problem. While we can spend time writing, testing and "
"applying lots of little changes, sometimes the right solution is to rebuild. "
"If a rebuild or refactor of a particular component has been proposed or is "
"underway, you may find that bugs affecting that component will not get as "
"much attention. Again, this is a matter of prioritizing scarce resources. By "
"concentrating on the rebuild, we can close all the little bugs at once, and "
"hopefully prevent other little bugs from appearing in the future."
msgstr ""
"Cúis eile go bhféadfaí neamhaird a dhéanamh ar fhabht ar feadh tamaill ná "
"más siomtóim d'fhadhb níos mó é an fabht. Cé gur féidir linn am a chaitheamh "
"ag scríobh, ag tástáil agus ag cur go leor athruithe beaga i bhfeidhm, "
"uaireanta is é an réiteach ceart ná atógáil. Má tá atógáil nó athfhriotal de "
"chomhpháirt ar leith molta nó ar siúl, b'fhéidir go bhfaighidh tú amach nach "
"dtabharfar an oiread airde ar fhabhtanna a théann i bhfeidhm ar an "
"gcomhpháirt sin. Arís, is ceist í seo a thugann tús áite d'acmhainní gann. "
"Trí dhíriú ar an atógáil, is féidir linn na fabhtanna beaga go léir a "
"dhúnadh ag an am céanna, agus tá súil againn cosc a chur ar fhabhtanna beaga "
"eile a bheith le feiceáil amach anseo."

msgid ""
"Whatever the reason, please keep in mind that while you may hit a particular "
"bug regularly, it doesn't necessarily follow that every single Django user "
"will hit the same bug. Different users use Django in different ways, "
"stressing different parts of the code under different conditions. When we "
"evaluate the relative priorities, we are generally trying to consider the "
"needs of the entire community, instead of prioritizing the impact on one "
"particular user. This doesn't mean that we think your problem is unimportant "
"-- just that in the limited time we have available, we will always err on "
"the side of making 10 people happy rather than making a single person happy."
msgstr ""
"Cibé cúis atá leis, coinnigh i gcuimhne, cé gur féidir leat fabht áirithe a "
"bhualadh go rialta, ní gá go leanfaidh sé go mbuailfidh gach úsáideoir "
"Django amháin an fabht céanna. Úsáideann úsáideoirí éagsúla Django ar "
"bhealaí éagsúla, ag cur béime ar chodanna éagsúla den chód faoi "
"choinníollacha éagsúla. Nuair a dhéanaimid meastóireacht ar na tosaíochtaí "
"coibhneasta, táimid ag iarraidh riachtanais an phobail ar fad a mheas go "
"ginearálta, seachas tús áite a thabhairt don tionchar ar úsáideoir amháin ar "
"leith. Ní chiallaíonn sé seo go gceapann muid go bhfuil d'fhadhb gan "
"tábhacht -- ach go bhfuil an t-am teoranta atá ar fáil againn, beidh muid i "
"gcónaí err ar an taobh a dhéanamh 10 daoine sásta seachas a dhéanamh duine "
"amháin sásta."

msgid ""
"I'm sure my ticket is absolutely 100% perfect, can I mark it as \"Ready For "
"Checkin\" myself?"
msgstr ""
"Tá mé cinnte go bhfuil mo thicéad go hiomlán 100% foirfe, an féidir liom é a "
"mharcáil mar \"Ready For Checkin\" mé féin?"

msgid ""
"Sorry, no. It's always better to get another set of eyes on a ticket. If "
"you're having trouble getting that second set of eyes, see questions above."
msgstr ""
"Tá brón orm, níl. Is fearr i gcónaí sraith súl eile a fháil ar thicéad. Má "
"tá deacracht agat an dara sraith súl sin a fháil, féach na ceisteanna thuas."

msgid "FAQ: General"
msgstr "Ceisteanna Coitianta: Ginearálta"

msgid "Why does this project exist?"
msgstr "Cén fáth a bhfuil an tionscadal seo ann?"

msgid ""
"Django grew from a very practical need: World Online, a newspaper web "
"operation, is responsible for building intensive web applications on "
"journalism deadlines. In the fast-paced newsroom, World Online often has "
"only a matter of hours to take a complicated web application from concept to "
"public launch."
msgstr ""
"D'fhás Django ó riachtanas an-phraiticiúil: Tá World Online, oibríocht "
"gréasáin nuachtáin, freagrach as dianiarratais ghréasáin a thógáil ar "
"spriocdhátaí iriseoireachta. Sa seomra nuachta luas tapa, is minic nach "
"mbíonn ach ceist uaireanta an chloig ag World Online chun feidhmchlár casta "
"gréasáin a ghlacadh ó choincheap go seoladh poiblí."

msgid ""
"At the same time, the World Online web developers have consistently been "
"perfectionists when it comes to following best practices of web development."
msgstr ""
"Ag an am céanna, bhí forbróirí gréasáin World Online ina foirfeoirí go "
"seasta nuair a thagann sé chun dea-chleachtais forbartha gréasáin a leanúint."

msgid ""
"In fall 2003, the World Online developers (Adrian Holovaty and Simon "
"Willison) ditched PHP and began using Python to develop its websites. As "
"they built intensive, richly interactive sites such as Lawrence.com, they "
"began to extract a generic web development framework that let them build web "
"applications more and more quickly. They tweaked this framework constantly, "
"adding improvements over two years."
msgstr ""
"Ag titim 2003, dhíbir forbróirí World Online (Adrian Holovaty agus Simon "
"Willison) PHP agus thosaigh siad ag baint úsáide as Python chun a láithreáin "
"ghréasáin a fhorbairt. De réir mar a thóg siad suíomhanna dian, "
"idirghníomhacha ar nós Lawrence.com, thosaigh siad ag baint creat forbartha "
"gréasáin cineálach a lig dóibh feidhmchláir ghréasáin a thógáil níos tapúla. "
"Rinne siad tweaked ar an gcreat seo i gcónaí, ag cur feabhsuithe thar dhá "
"bhliain."

msgid ""
"In summer 2005, World Online decided to open-source the resulting software, "
"Django. Django would not be possible without a whole host of open-source "
"projects -- `Apache`_, `Python`_, and `PostgreSQL`_ to name a few -- and "
"we're thrilled to be able to give something back to the open-source "
"community."
msgstr ""
"I samhradh na bliana 2005, chinn World Online na bogearraí a bhí mar thoradh "
"air a oscailt, Django. Ní bheadh Django indéanta gan a lán tionscadal foinse "
"oscailte -- 'Apache'_, 'Python'_, agus 'PostgreSQL'_ chun cúpla -- a ainmniú "
"agus tá áthas orainn a bheith in ann rud éigin a thabhairt ar ais don phobal "
"foinse oscailte."

msgid "What does \"Django\" mean, and how do you pronounce it?"
msgstr "Cad a chiallaíonn \"Django\", agus conas a fhuaimníonn tú é?"

msgid ""
"Django is named after `Django Reinhardt`_, a jazz manouche guitarist from "
"the 1930s to early 1950s. To this day, he's considered one of the best "
"guitarists of all time."
msgstr ""
"Tá Django ainmnithe i ndiaidh 'Django Reinhardt'_, giotáraí manouche "
"snagcheoil ó na 1930idí go dtí tús na 1950idí. Go dtí an lá atá inniu ann, "
"meastar go bhfuil sé ar dhuine de na giotáraithe is fearr riamh."

msgid "Listen to his music. You'll like it."
msgstr "Éist lena chuid ceoil. Taitneoidh sé leat."

msgid ""
"Django is pronounced **JANG**-oh. Rhymes with FANG-oh. The \"D\" is silent."
msgstr "Fuaimnítear Django **JANG **-oh. Rannta le FANG-OH. Tá an \"D\" ciúin."

msgid "We've also recorded an `audio clip of the pronunciation`_."
msgstr "Tá 'gearrthóg fuaime den fhuaimniú' taifeadta againn freisin_."

msgid "Is Django stable?"
msgstr "An bhfuil Django cobhsaí?"

msgid ""
"Yes, it's quite stable. Companies like Disqus, Instagram, Pinterest, and "
"Mozilla have been using Django for many years. Sites built on Django have "
"weathered traffic spikes of over 50 thousand hits per second."
msgstr ""
"Sea, tá sé cobhsaí go leor. Tá cuideachtaí cosúil le Disqus, Instagram, "
"Pinterest, agus Mozilla ag baint úsáide as Django le blianta fada. Tá spící "
"tráchta de níos mó ná 50 míle amas in aghaidh an tsoicind ag láithreáin a "
"tógadh ar Django."

msgid "Does Django scale?"
msgstr "An scálaíonn Django?"

msgid ""
"Yes. Compared to development time, hardware is cheap, and so Django is "
"designed to take advantage of as much hardware as you can throw at it."
msgstr ""
"Tá. I gcomparáid le ham forbartha, tá crua-earraí saor, agus mar sin tá "
"Django deartha chun leas a bhaint as an oiread crua-earraí agus is féidir "
"leat a chaitheamh air."

msgid ""
"Django uses a \"shared-nothing\" architecture, which means you can add "
"hardware at any level -- database servers, caching servers or web/"
"application servers."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann Django ailtireacht \"rud ar bith comhroinnte\", rud a chiallaíonn "
"gur féidir leat crua-earraí a chur leis ag aon leibhéal - freastalaithe "
"bunachar sonraí, freastalaithe caching nó freastalaithe gréasáin / "
"feidhmchláir."

msgid ""
"The framework cleanly separates components such as its database layer and "
"application layer. And it ships with a simple-yet-powerful :doc:`cache "
"framework </topics/cache>`."
msgstr ""
"Scarann an creat comhpháirteanna go glan, mar shampla a chiseal bunachar "
"sonraí agus a chiseal feidhmchláir. Agus longa sé le simplí-fós-"
"chumhachtach :d oc: 'creat taisce < / topaicí / taisce>'."

msgid "Who's behind this?"
msgstr "Cé atá taobh thiar de seo?"

msgid ""
"Django was originally developed at World Online, the web department of a "
"newspaper in Lawrence, Kansas, USA. Django's now run by an international "
"`team of volunteers <https://www.djangoproject.com/foundation/teams/>`_."
msgstr ""
"Forbraíodh Django ar dtús ag World Online, roinn gréasáin nuachtáin i "
"Lawrence, Kansas, SAM. Tá Django á reáchtáil anois ag 'foireann "
"idirnáisiúnta oibrithe deonacha <https://www.djangoproject.com/foundation/"
"teams/>'_."

msgid "How is Django licensed?"
msgstr "Conas atá Django ceadúnaithe?"

msgid ""
"Django is distributed under :source:`the 3-clause BSD license <LICENSE>`. "
"This is an open source license granting broad permissions to modify and "
"redistribute Django."
msgstr ""
"Django dháileadh faoi:foinse:'an ceadúnas BSD 3-clásal<LICENSE>'. Is "
"ceadúnas foinse oscailte é seo a thugann ceadanna leathana chun Django a "
"mhodhnú agus a athdháileadh."

msgid "Why does Django include Python's license file?"
msgstr "Cén fáth a n-áiríonn Django comhad ceadúnais Python?"

msgid ""
"Django includes code from the Python standard library. Python is distributed "
"under a permissive open source license. :source:`A copy of the Python "
"license <LICENSE.python>` is included with Django for compliance with "
"Python's terms."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn Django cód ó leabharlann chaighdeánach Python. Dáiltear Python "
"faoi cheadúnas foinse oscailte ceadaitheach. :foinse:'Tá cóip den cheadúnas "
"Python <LICENSE.python>' san áireamh le Django chun téarmaí Python a "
"chomhlíonadh."

msgid "Which sites use Django?"
msgstr "Cé na suíomhanna a úsáideann Django?"

msgid ""
"`BuiltWithDjango.com`_ features a constantly growing list of Django-powered "
"sites."
msgstr ""
"Tá liosta de shuíomhanna faoi thiomáint Django ag fás i gcónaí ar "
"'BuiltWithDjango.com'_."

msgid ""
"Django appears to be a MVC framework, but you call the Controller the "
"\"view\", and the View the \"template\". How come you don't use the standard "
"names?"
msgstr ""
"Is cosúil gur creat MVC é Django, ach glaonn tú ar an Rialaitheoir an "
"\"dearcadh\", agus an Féach ar an \"teimpléad\". Cén chaoi nach n-úsáideann "
"tú na hainmneacha caighdeánacha?"

msgid "Well, the standard names are debatable."
msgstr "Bhuel, tá na hainmneacha caighdeánacha díospóireachta."

msgid ""
"In our interpretation of MVC, the \"view\" describes the data that gets "
"presented to the user. It's not necessarily *how* the data *looks*, but "
"*which* data is presented. The view describes *which data you see*, not *how "
"you see it.* It's a subtle distinction."
msgstr ""
"Inár léirmhíniú ar MVC, déanann an \"dearcadh\" cur síos ar na sonraí a "
"chuirtear i láthair an úsáideora. Ní gá *conas * na sonraí *Breathnaíonn *, "
"ach *a * sonraí i láthair. Déanann an t-amharc cur síos ar *na sonraí a "
"fheiceann tú *, ní *conas a fheiceann tú é.* Is idirdhealú caolchúiseach é."

msgid ""
"So, in our case, a \"view\" is the Python callback function for a particular "
"URL, because that callback function describes which data is presented."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin, inár gcás, is é \"amharc\" an fheidhm aisghlaoigh Python le "
"haghaidh URL ar leith, toisc go ndéanann an fheidhm aisghlaoigh sin cur síos "
"ar na sonraí a chuirtear i láthair."

msgid ""
"Furthermore, it's sensible to separate content from presentation -- which is "
"where templates come in. In Django, a \"view\" describes which data is "
"presented, but a view normally delegates to a template, which describes "
"*how* the data is presented."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, tá sé ciallmhar ábhar a scaradh ó chur i láthair - is é "
"sin an áit a dtagann teimpléid isteach. In Django, déanann \"dearcadh\" cur "
"síos ar na sonraí a chuirtear i láthair, ach de ghnáth toscairí dearcadh "
"chuig teimpléad, a chuireann síos ar *conas * a chuirtear na sonraí i "
"láthair."

msgid ""
"Where does the \"controller\" fit in, then? In Django's case, it's probably "
"the framework itself: the machinery that sends a request to the appropriate "
"view, according to the Django URL configuration."
msgstr ""
"Cá bhfuil an \"rialtóir\" oiriúnach, ansin? I gcás Django, is dócha gurb é "
"an creat féin é: an t-innealra a sheolann iarratas chuig an dearcadh cuí, de "
"réir chumraíocht URL Django."

msgid ""
"If you're hungry for acronyms, you might say that Django is a \"MTV\" "
"framework -- that is, \"model\", \"template\", and \"view.\" That breakdown "
"makes much more sense."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ocras ort le haghaidh acrainmneacha, d'fhéadfá a rá gur creat \"MTV\" "
"é Django - is é sin, \"samhail\", \"teimpléad\", agus \"amharc.\" Tá ciall i "
"bhfad níos mó leis an miondealú sin."

msgid ""
"At the end of the day, it comes down to getting stuff done. And, regardless "
"of how things are named, Django gets stuff done in a way that's most logical "
"to us."
msgstr ""
"Ag deireadh an lae, tagann sé anuas chun rudaí a dhéanamh. Agus, beag beann "
"ar an gcaoi a n-ainmnítear rudaí, faigheann Django rudaí a dhéantar ar "
"bhealach is loighciúla dúinn."

msgid "<Framework X> does <feature Y> -- why doesn't Django?"
msgstr "<Creat X> a dhéanann <gné Y> -- cén fáth nach bhfuil Django?"

msgid ""
"We're well aware that there are other awesome web frameworks out there, and "
"we're not averse to borrowing ideas where appropriate. However, Django was "
"developed precisely because we were unhappy with the status quo, so please "
"be aware that \"because <Framework X> does it\" is not going to be "
"sufficient reason to add a given feature to Django."
msgstr ""
"Tá a fhios againn go maith go bhfuil creataí gréasáin uamhnach eile ann, "
"agus nílimid in ann smaointe a fháil ar iasacht nuair is cuí. Mar sin féin, "
"forbraíodh Django go beacht toisc go raibh muid míshásta leis an status quo, "
"mar sin bí ar an eolas nach leor \"toisc nach bhfuil <Framework X> a "
"dhéanann sé\" ina chúis leordhóthanach chun gné áirithe a chur le Django."

msgid ""
"Why did you write all of Django from scratch, instead of using other Python "
"libraries?"
msgstr ""
"Cén fáth ar scríobh tú Django ar fad ó thús, seachas leabharlanna Python "
"eile a úsáid?"

msgid ""
"When Django was originally written, Adrian and Simon spent quite a bit of "
"time exploring the various Python web frameworks available."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a scríobhadh Django ar dtús, chaith Adrian agus Simon go leor ama ag "
"iniúchadh na gcreataí gréasáin éagsúla Python atá ar fáil."

msgid "In our opinion, none of them were completely up to snuff."
msgstr "Is é ár dtuairim nach raibh aon cheann acu go hiomlán suas le snaois."

msgid "We're picky. You might even call us perfectionists. (With deadlines.)"
msgstr ""
"Táimid piocúil. D'fhéadfá fiú perfectionists glaoch orainn. (Le "
"spriocdhátaí.)"

msgid ""
"Over time, we stumbled across open-source libraries that did things we'd "
"already implemented. It was reassuring to see other people solving similar "
"problems in similar ways, but it was too late to integrate outside code: "
"We'd already written, tested and implemented our own framework bits in "
"several production settings -- and our own code met our needs delightfully."
msgstr ""
"Le himeacht ama, shiúil muid ar fud leabharlanna foinse oscailte a rinne "
"rudaí a bhí curtha i bhfeidhm againn cheana féin. Bhí sé dearfach a "
"fheiceáil daoine eile a réiteach fadhbanna den chineál céanna ar bhealaí den "
"chineál céanna, ach bhí sé ró-dhéanach a chomhtháthú cód lasmuigh: Ba mhaith "
"linn a scríobh cheana féin, a thástáil agus a chur i bhfeidhm ár giotán "
"creat féin i suímh táirgthe éagsúla - agus ár gcód féin freastal ar ár "
"riachtanais delightfully."

msgid ""
"In most cases, however, we found that existing frameworks/tools inevitably "
"had some sort of fundamental, fatal flaw that made us squeamish. No tool fit "
"our philosophies 100%."
msgstr ""
"I bhformhór na gcásanna, áfach, fuaireamar amach go raibh locht bunúsach, "
"marfach de chineál éigin ar chreataí/uirlisí atá ann cheana féin a d'fhág go "
"raibh muid squeamish. Níl aon uirlis oiriúnach dár bhfealsúnachtaí 100%."

msgid "Like we said: We're picky."
msgstr "Mar a dúirt muid: Táimid piocúil."

msgid ""
"We've documented our philosophies on the :doc:`design philosophies page </"
"misc/design-philosophies>`."
msgstr ""
"Tá doiciméadú déanta againn ar ár bhfealsúnachtaí ar an leathanach :d "
"oc:'design philosophies </misc/design-philosophies>'."

msgid "Is Django a content-management-system (CMS)?"
msgstr "An córas bainistíochta inneachair (CMS) é Django?"

msgid ""
"No, Django is not a CMS, or any sort of \"turnkey product\" in and of "
"itself. It's a web framework; it's a programming tool that lets you build "
"websites."
msgstr ""
"Níl, ní CMS é Django, nó aon chineál \"táirge turnkey\" ann féin agus as "
"féin. Is creat gréasáin é; is uirlis ríomhchláraithe é a ligeann duit "
"láithreáin ghréasáin a thógáil."

msgid ""
"For example, it doesn't make much sense to compare Django to something like "
"Drupal_, because Django is something you use to *create* things like Drupal."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, ní dhéanann sé mórán céille Django a chur i gcomparáid le rud "
"éigin cosúil le Drupal_, toisc gur rud é Django a úsáideann tú chun rudaí *a "
"chruthú * cosúil le Drupal."

msgid ""
"Yes, Django's automatic admin site is fantastic and timesaving -- but the "
"admin site is one module of Django the framework. Furthermore, although "
"Django has special conveniences for building \"CMS-y\" apps, that doesn't "
"mean it's not just as appropriate for building \"non-CMS-y\" apps (whatever "
"that means!)."
msgstr ""
"Sea, tá suíomh riaracháin uathoibríoch Django iontach agus timesaving - ach "
"is é an suíomh riaracháin modúl amháin de Django an creat. Ina theannta sin, "
"cé go bhfuil áiseanna speisialta ag Django chun feidhmchláir \"CMS-y\" a "
"thógáil, ní chiallaíonn sé sin nach bhfuil sé chomh hoiriúnach chun "
"feidhmchláir \"neamh-CMS-y\" a thógáil (is cuma cad a chiallaíonn sé sin!)."

msgid "How can I download the Django documentation to read it offline?"
msgstr ""
"Conas is féidir liom doiciméadú Django a íoslódáil chun é a léamh as líne?"

msgid ""
"The Django docs are available in the ``docs`` directory of each Django "
"tarball release. These docs are in reST (reStructuredText) format, and each "
"text file corresponds to a web page on the official Django site."
msgstr ""
"Tá docs Django ar fáil san eolaire ''docs'' de gach eisiúint tarball Django. "
"Tá na docs seo i bhformáid reST (reStructuredText), agus freagraíonn gach "
"comhad téacs do leathanach gréasáin ar shuíomh oifigiúil Django."

msgid ""
"Because the documentation is :source:`stored in revision control <docs>`, "
"you can browse documentation changes just like you can browse code changes."
msgstr ""
"Toisc go bhfuil an doiciméadú: foinse: 'stóráilte i rialú "
"athbhreithnithe<docs>', is féidir leat athruithe doiciméadaithe a bhrabhsáil "
"díreach mar is féidir leat athruithe cód a bhrabhsáil."

msgid ""
"Technically, the docs on Django's site are generated from the latest "
"development versions of those reST documents, so the docs on the Django site "
"may offer more information than the docs that come with the latest Django "
"release."
msgstr ""
"Go teicniúil, gintear na docs ar shuíomh Django ó na leaganacha forbartha is "
"déanaí de na doiciméid reST sin, mar sin d'fhéadfadh na docs ar shuíomh "
"Django níos mó faisnéise a thairiscint ná na docs a thagann leis an "
"scaoileadh Django is déanaí."

msgid "How do I cite Django?"
msgstr "Conas is féidir liom Django a lua?"

msgid ""
"It's difficult to give an official citation format, for two reasons: "
"citation formats can vary wildly between publications, and citation "
"standards for software are still a matter of some debate."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé deacair formáid oifigiúil lua a thabhairt, ar dhá chúis: is féidir le "
"formáidí lua a bheith éagsúil go fiáin idir foilseacháin, agus tá caighdeáin "
"lua do bhogearraí fós ina ábhar díospóireachta éigin."

msgid "For example, `APA style`_,  would dictate something like:"
msgstr "Mar shampla, bheadh 'stíl APA'_, rud éigin cosúil le:"

msgid ""
"However, the only true guide is what your publisher will accept, so get a "
"copy of those guidelines and fill in the gaps as best you can."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, is é an t-aon treoir fíor ná an méid a ghlacfaidh "
"d'fhoilsitheoir leis, mar sin faigh cóip de na treoirlínte sin agus líon "
"isteach na bearnaí is fearr is féidir leat."

msgid ""
"If your referencing style guide requires a publisher name, use \"Django "
"Software Foundation\"."
msgstr ""
"Má theastaíonn ainm foilsitheora ó do threoir stíle tagartha, bain úsáid as "
"\"Django Software Foundation\"."

msgid "If you need a publishing location, use \"Lawrence, Kansas\"."
msgstr ""
"Má theastaíonn suíomh foilsitheoireachta uait, bain úsáid as \"Lawrence, "
"Kansas\"."

msgid "If you need a web address, use https://www.djangoproject.com/."
msgstr ""
"Má theastaíonn seoladh gréasáin uait, bain úsáid as https://"
"www.djangoproject.com/."

msgid "If you need a name, just use \"Django\", without any tagline."
msgstr "Má theastaíonn ainm uait, bain úsáid as \"Django\", gan aon chliblíne."

msgid ""
"If you need a publication date, use the year of release of the version "
"you're referencing (e.g., 2013 for v1.5)"
msgstr ""
"Má theastaíonn dáta foilsithe uait, bain úsáid as bliain scaoilte an leagain "
"a bhfuil tú ag tagairt dó (m.sh., 2013 le haghaidh v1.5)"

msgid "Where can I find more Django resources?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Steering Council maintains a collection of Django third-party packages, "
"organizations and resources at https://www.djangoproject.com/community/"
"ecosystem/."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"That page will be updated to contain links to various Django content such as "
"podcasts, videos, conferences, blogs, books, and learning resources. It also "
"features popular, robust, community-maintained packages."
msgstr ""

msgid "FAQ: Getting Help"
msgstr "Ceisteanna Coitianta: Cabhair a Fháil"

msgid "How do I do X? Why doesn't Y work? Where can I go to get help?"
msgstr ""
"Conas a dhéanaim X? Cén fáth nach n-oibríonn Y? Cá háit is féidir liom dul "
"chun cabhair a fháil?"

msgid ""
"First, please check if your question is answered on the :doc:`FAQ </faq/"
"index>`. Also, search for answers using your favorite search engine, and in "
"`the forum`_."
msgstr ""
"Ar dtús, seiceáil le do thoil an bhfuil freagra ar do cheist ar an :d "
"oc:'Ceisteanna Coitianta </faq/index>'. Chomh maith leis sin, cuardaigh "
"freagraí ag baint úsáide as an inneall cuardaigh is fearr leat, agus i 'an "
"fóram'_."

msgid ""
"If you can't find an answer, please take a few minutes to formulate your "
"question well. Explaining the problems you are facing clearly will help "
"others help you. See the StackOverflow guide on `asking good questions`_."
msgstr ""
"Mura féidir leat freagra a fháil, tóg cúpla nóiméad le do cheist a chur le "
"chéile go maith. Má mhíníonn tú na fadhbanna atá romhat go soiléir, "
"cabhróidh sé le daoine eile cabhrú leat. Féach an treoir StackOverflow ar "
"'ceisteanna maithe a chur'_."

msgid "Then, please post it in one of the following channels:"
msgstr "Ansin, cuir sa phost é i gceann de na bealaí seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"The Django Forum section `\"Using Django\"`_. This is for web-based "
"discussions."
msgstr ""
"Rannóg Fhóram Django '\"Ag baint úsáide as Django\"'_. Tá sé seo le haghaidh "
"plé gréasán-bhunaithe."

msgid "The `Django Discord server`_ for chat-based discussions."
msgstr "An 'Django Discord server'_ le haghaidh plé comhrá-bhunaithe."

msgid ""
"In all these channels please abide by the `Django Code of Conduct`_. In "
"summary, being friendly and patient, considerate, respectful, and careful in "
"your choice of words."
msgstr ""
"Sna bealaí seo go léir cloí le 'Cód Iompair Django'_. Go hachomair, a bheith "
"cairdiúil agus foighneach, tuisceanach, measúil, agus cúramach i do rogha "
"focal."

msgid "Nobody answered my question! What should I do?"
msgstr "Níor fhreagair aon duine mo cheist! Céard ba chóir dom a dhéanamh?"

msgid ""
"Try making your question more specific, or provide a better example of your "
"problem."
msgstr ""
"Bain triail as do cheist a dhéanamh níos sainiúla, nó tabhair sampla níos "
"fearr de d'fhadhb."

msgid ""
"As with most open-source projects, the folks on these channels are "
"volunteers. If nobody has answered your question, it may be because nobody "
"knows the answer, it may be because nobody can understand the question, or "
"it may be that everybody that can help is busy."
msgstr ""
"Mar aon leis an gcuid is mó de na tionscadail foinse oscailte, is oibrithe "
"deonacha iad na daoine ar na bealaí seo. Má tá aon duine freagra do cheist, "
"d'fhéadfadh sé a bheith toisc go bhfuil a fhios ag aon duine an freagra, "
"d'fhéadfadh sé a bheith toisc gur féidir aon duine a thuiscint an cheist, nó "
"d'fhéadfadh sé a bheith go bhfuil gach duine gur féidir cabhrú gnóthach."

msgid ""
"You can also try asking on a different channel. But please don't post your "
"question in all three channels in quick succession."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat iarracht a dhéanamh freisin iarraidh ar chainéal eile. Ach ná "
"cuir do cheist sa phost i ngach ceann de na trí chainéal i ndiaidh a chéile "
"go tapa."

msgid "I think I've found a bug! What should I do?"
msgstr "Sílim go bhfuil fabht aimsithe agam! Céard ba chóir dom a dhéanamh?"

msgid ""
"Detailed instructions on how to handle a potential bug can be found in "
"our :ref:`Guide to contributing to Django <reporting-bugs>`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir treoracha mionsonraithe maidir le conas fabht féideartha a "
"láimhseáil a fháil inár :ref:'Guide to contributing to Django<reporting-"
"bugs>'."

msgid "I think I've found a security problem! What should I do?"
msgstr ""
"Sílim go bhfuil fadhb slándála aimsithe agam! Céard ba chóir dom a dhéanamh?"

msgid ""
"If you think you've found a security problem with Django, please send a "
"message to security@djangoproject.com. This is a private list only open to "
"long-time, highly trusted Django developers, and its archives are not "
"publicly readable."
msgstr ""
"Má cheapann tú go bhfuil fadhb slándála aimsithe agat le Django, seol "
"teachtaireacht chuig security@djangoproject.com. Is liosta príobháideach é "
"seo nach bhfuil oscailte ach d'fhorbróirí Django le fada an lá, agus níl a "
"chartlanna inléite go poiblí."

msgid ""
"Due to the sensitive nature of security issues, we ask that if you think you "
"have found a security problem, *please* don't post a message on the forum, "
"the Discord server, IRC, or one of the public mailing lists. Django has "
"a :ref:`policy for handling security issues <reporting-security-issues>`; "
"while a defect is outstanding, we would like to minimize any damage that "
"could be inflicted through public knowledge of that defect."
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar nádúr íogair na saincheisteanna slándála, iarraimid má "
"cheapann tú go bhfuil fadhb slándála aimsithe agat, *le do thoil * ná cuir "
"teachtaireacht ar an bhfóram, ar an bhfreastalaí Discord, ar IRC, nó ar "
"cheann de na liostaí poist poiblí. Tá :ref:'policy for handling security "
"issues' ag Django<reporting-security-issues>; cé go bhfuil locht gan íoc, ba "
"mhaith linn aon damáiste a d'fhéadfaí a dhéanamh trí eolas an phobail ar an "
"locht sin a íoslaghdú."

msgid "Django FAQ"
msgstr "Ceisteanna Coitianta Django"

msgid "FAQ: Installation"
msgstr "Ceisteanna Coitianta: Suiteáil"

msgid "How do I get started?"
msgstr "Conas is féidir liom tosú?"

msgid "`Download the code`_."
msgstr "'Íoslódáil an cód'_."

msgid "Install Django (read the :doc:`installation guide </intro/install>`)."
msgstr ""
"Suiteáil Django (léigh an :d oc: 'installation guide </intro/install>')."

msgid "Walk through the :doc:`tutorial </intro/tutorial01>`."
msgstr "Siúil tríd an :d oc:'tutorial </intro/tutorial01>'."

msgid ""
"Check out the rest of the :doc:`documentation </index>`, and `ask "
"questions`_ if you run into trouble."
msgstr ""
"Amharc ar an gcuid eile den :d oc:'documentation </index>', agus 'cuir "
"ceisteanna'_ má bhíonn tú i dtrioblóid."

msgid "What are Django's prerequisites?"
msgstr "Cad iad réamhriachtanais Django?"

msgid ""
"Django requires Python. See the table in the next question for the versions "
"of Python that work with each version of Django. Other Python libraries may "
"be required for some use cases, but you'll receive an error about them as "
"they're needed."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn Django Python. Féach an tábla sa chéad cheist eile do na leaganacha "
"de Python a oibríonn le gach leagan de Django. D'fhéadfadh leabharlanna "
"Python eile a bheith ag teastáil le haghaidh roinnt cásanna úsáide, ach "
"gheobhaidh tú earráid fúthu de réir mar a theastaíonn siad."

msgid ""
"For a development environment -- if you just want to experiment with Django "
"-- you don't need to have a separate web server installed or database server."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh timpeallacht forbartha - más mian leat triail a bhaint as Django "
"- ní gá duit freastalaí gréasáin ar leith a bheith suiteáilte nó freastalaí "
"bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"Django comes with its own :djadmin:`lightweight development "
"server<runserver>`. For a production environment, Django follows the WSGI "
"spec, :pep:`3333`, which means it can run on a variety of web servers. "
"See :doc:`Deploying Django </howto/deployment/index>` for more information."
msgstr ""
"Tagann Django lena :d jadmin: 'freastalaí forbartha lightweight' "
"féin<runserver>. Maidir le timpeallacht táirgthe, leanann Django spec "
"WSGI, :p ep: '3333', rud a chiallaíonn gur féidir é a reáchtáil ar "
"fhreastalaithe gréasáin éagsúla. Féach :d oc:'Deploying Django </howto/"
"deployment/index>' le haghaidh tuilleadh eolais."

msgid ""
"Django runs `SQLite`_ by default, which is included in Python installations. "
"For a production environment, we recommend PostgreSQL_; but we also "
"officially support MariaDB_, MySQL_, `SQLite`_, and Oracle_. "
"See :doc:`Supported Databases </ref/databases>` for more information."
msgstr ""
"Ritheann Django 'SQLite' _ de réir réamhshocraithe, atá san áireamh i "
"suiteálacha Python. I gcás timpeallacht táirgthe, molaimid PostgreSQL_; ach "
"tacaímid go hoifigiúil freisin MariaDB_, MySQL_, 'SQLite'_, agus Oracle_. "
"Féach :d oc:'Bunachair Shonraí Tacaithe </ref/databases>' le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh eolais."

msgid "What Python version can I use with Django?"
msgstr "Cén leagan Python is féidir liom a úsáid le Django?"

msgid "Django version"
msgstr "Leagan Django"

msgid "Python versions"
msgstr "Leaganacha Python"

msgid "4.2"
msgstr "4.2"

msgid "3.8, 3.9, 3.10, 3.11, 3.12 (added in 4.2.8)"
msgstr "3.8, 3.9, 3.10, 3.11, 3.12 (arna chur leis in 4.2.8)"

msgid "5.0"
msgstr "5.0"

msgid "3.10, 3.11, 3.12"
msgstr "3.10, 3.11, 3.12"

msgid "5.1"
msgstr "5.1"

msgid "3.10, 3.11, 3.12, 3.13 (added in 5.1.3)"
msgstr "3.10, 3.11, 3.12, 3.13 (arna chur leis in 5.1.3)"

msgid "5.2"
msgstr ""

msgid "3.10, 3.11, 3.12, 3.13, 3.14 (added in 5.2.8)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For each version of Python, only the latest micro release (A.B.C) is "
"officially supported. Python versions that have reached end-of-life are no "
"longer maintained by the Python project and therefore should not be used "
"with Django."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can find the latest supported micro version for each series on the "
"`Python download page <https://www.python.org/downloads/>`_."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We will support a Python version up to and including the first Django LTS "
"release whose security support ends after security support for that version "
"of Python ends. For example, Python 3.9 security support ends in October "
"2025 and Django 4.2 LTS security support ends in April 2026. Therefore "
"Django 4.2 is the last version to support Python 3.9."
msgstr ""

msgid "What Python version should I use with Django?"
msgstr "Cén leagan Python ba chóir dom a úsáid le Django?"

msgid ""
"Since newer versions of Python are often faster, have more features, and are "
"better supported, the latest version of Python 3 is recommended."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go mbíonn leaganacha níos nuaí de Python níos tapúla go minic, go "
"bhfuil níos mó gnéithe acu, agus go dtugtar tacaíocht níos fearr dóibh, "
"moltar an leagan is déanaí de Python 3."

msgid ""
"You don't lose anything in Django by using an older release, but you don't "
"take advantage of the improvements and optimizations in newer Python "
"releases. Third-party applications for use with Django are free to set their "
"own version requirements."
msgstr ""
"Ní chailleann tú aon rud i Django trí scaoileadh níos sine a úsáid, ach ní "
"bhaineann tú leas as na feabhsuithe agus na barrfheabhsuithe i eisiúintí "
"Python níos nuaí. Tá iarratais tríú páirtí lena n-úsáid le Django saor in "
"aisce chun a gcuid riachtanas leagan féin a shocrú."

msgid "Should I use the stable version or development version?"
msgstr "Ar cheart dom an leagan cobhsaí nó an leagan forbartha a úsáid?"

msgid ""
"Generally, if you're using code in production, you should be using a stable "
"release. The Django project publishes a full stable release every eight "
"months or so, with bugfix updates in between. These stable releases contain "
"the API that is covered by our backwards compatibility guarantees; if you "
"write code against stable releases, you shouldn't have any problems "
"upgrading when the next official version is released."
msgstr ""
"Go ginearálta, má tá cód á úsáid agat i dtáirgeadh, ba chóir duit a bheith "
"ag baint úsáide as scaoileadh cobhsaí. Foilsíonn tionscadal Django "
"scaoileadh cobhsaí iomlán gach ocht mí nó mar sin, le nuashonruithe bugfix "
"idir eatarthu. Cuimsíonn na heisiúintí cobhsaí seo an API atá clúdaithe ag "
"ár ráthaíochtaí comhoiriúnachta ar gcúl; Má scríobhann tú cód i gcoinne "
"eisiúintí cobhsaí, níor chóir go mbeadh aon fhadhbanna agat uasghrádú nuair "
"a scaoiltear an chéad leagan oifigiúil eile."

msgid "FAQ: Databases and models"
msgstr "Ceisteanna Coitianta: Bunachair shonraí agus samhlacha"

msgid "How can I see the raw SQL queries Django is running?"
msgstr ""
"Conas is féidir liom a fheiceáil go bhfuil na ceisteanna SQL amh Django ag "
"rith?"

msgid ""
"Make sure your Django :setting:`DEBUG` setting is set to ``True``. Then do "
"this:"
msgstr ""
"Cinntigh go bhfuil do shuíomh Django :setting:'DEBUG' socraithe go ''True''. "
"Ansin déan é seo:"

msgid ""
"``connection.queries`` is only available if :setting:`DEBUG` is ``True``. "
"It's a list of dictionaries in order of query execution. Each dictionary has "
"the following:"
msgstr ""
"Níl ''connection.queries'' ar fáil ach amháin má tá :setting:'DEBUG' is "
"''Fíor''. Is liosta foclóirí é in ord forghníomhú an fhiosraithe. Tá an méid "
"seo a leanas i ngach foclóir:"

msgid "``sql`` - The raw SQL statement"
msgstr "''sql'' - An ráiteas SQL amh"

msgid "``time`` - How long the statement took to execute, in seconds."
msgstr "''time'' - Cá fhad a thóg an ráiteas a fhorghníomhú, i soicindí."

msgid ""
"``connection.queries`` includes all SQL statements -- INSERTs, UPDATES, "
"SELECTs, etc. Each time your app hits the database, the query will be "
"recorded."
msgstr ""
"Folaíonn ''connection.queries'' gach ráiteas SQL -- INSERTs, UPDATES, "
"SELECTs, etc. Gach uair a bhuaileann d'aip an bunachar sonraí, déanfar an "
"cheist a thaifeadadh."

msgid ""
"If you are using :doc:`multiple databases</topics/db/multi-db>`, you can use "
"the same interface on each member of the ``connections`` dictionary:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag úsáid :d oc:'ilbhunachair shonraí</topics/db/multi-db>', is "
"féidir leat an comhéadan céanna a úsáid ar gach ball den fhoclóir ''naisc'':"

msgid ""
"If you need to clear the query list manually at any point in your functions, "
"call ``reset_queries()``, like this::"
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit an liosta ceisteanna a ghlanadh de láimh ag pointe ar bith i "
"d'fheidhmeanna, glaoigh ar ''reset_queries()'', mar seo::"

msgid "Can I use Django with a preexisting database?"
msgstr "An féidir liom Django a úsáid le bunachar sonraí preexisting?"

msgid ""
"Yes. See :doc:`Integrating with a legacy database </howto/legacy-databases>`."
msgstr ""
"Tá. Féach :d oc:'Comhtháthú le bunachar sonraí oidhreachta </howto/legacy-"
"databases>'."

msgid "If I make changes to a model, how do I update the database?"
msgstr ""
"Má dhéanaim athruithe ar mhúnla, conas is féidir liom an bunachar sonraí a "
"nuashonrú?"

msgid ""
"Take a look at Django's support for :mod:`schema migrations "
"<django.db.migrations>`."
msgstr ""
"Féach ar thacaíocht Django do:mod:'schema migrations <django.db.migrations>'."

msgid ""
"If you don't mind clearing data, your project's ``manage.py`` utility has "
"a :djadmin:`flush` option to reset the database to the state it was in "
"immediately after :djadmin:`migrate` was executed."
msgstr ""
"Mura miste leat sonraí a ghlanadh, tá rogha :d jadmin:'flush' ag fóntais "
"''manage.py' do thionscadail chun an bunachar sonraí a athshocrú chuig an "
"stát ina raibh sé díreach tar éis :d jadmin:'migrate' a fhorghníomhú."

msgid "Do Django models support multiple-column primary keys?"
msgstr "An dtacaíonn samhlacha Django le heochracha bunscoile ilcholúin?"

msgid "No. Only single-column primary keys are supported."
msgstr "Ní hea. Ní thacaítear ach le heochracha bunscoile aon cholúin."

msgid ""
"But this isn't an issue in practice, because there's nothing stopping you "
"from adding other constraints (using the ``unique_together`` model option or "
"creating the constraint directly in your database), and enforcing the "
"uniqueness at that level. Single-column primary keys are needed for things "
"such as the admin interface to work; e.g., you need a single value to "
"specify an object to edit or delete."
msgstr ""
"Ach ní ceist í seo go praiticiúil, mar níl aon rud ag cur stop leat ó "
"shrianta eile a chur leis (ag baint úsáide as an rogha samhail "
"''unique_together'' nó an srian a chruthú go díreach i do bhunachar sonraí), "
"agus an uathúlacht a fhorfheidhmiú ag an leibhéal sin. Tá eochracha "
"bunscoile aon-cholún ag teastáil le haghaidh rudaí cosúil leis an gcomhéadan "
"riaracháin a bheith ag obair; m.sh., ní mór duit luach amháin a shonrú rud a "
"chur in eagar nó a scriosadh."

msgid "Does Django support NoSQL databases?"
msgstr "An dtacaíonn Django le bunachair shonraí NoSQL?"

msgid ""
"NoSQL databases are not officially supported by Django itself. There are, "
"however, a number of side projects and forks which allow NoSQL functionality "
"in Django."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaíonn Django féin go hoifigiúil le bunachair shonraí NoSQL. Tá roinnt "
"tionscadal taobh agus forcanna ann, áfach, a cheadaíonn feidhmiúlacht NoSQL "
"i Django."

msgid "You can take a look on `the wiki page`_ which discusses some projects."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat breathnú ar 'an leathanach wiki'_ a phléann roinnt tionscadal."

msgid ""
"How do I add database-specific options to my CREATE TABLE statements, such "
"as specifying MyISAM as the table type?"
msgstr ""
"Conas is féidir liom roghanna a bhaineann go sonrach le bunachar sonraí a "
"chur le mo ráitis CREATE TABLE, mar shampla MyISAM a shonrú mar an cineál "
"tábla?"

msgid ""
"We try to avoid adding special cases in the Django code to accommodate all "
"the database-specific options such as table type, etc. If you'd like to use "
"any of these options, create a migration with "
"a :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RunSQL` operation that contains "
"``ALTER TABLE`` statements that do what you want to do."
msgstr ""
"Déanaimid iarracht gan cásanna speisialta a chur leis an gcód Django chun "
"freastal ar na roghanna go léir a bhaineann go sonrach le bunachar sonraí, "
"mar shampla cineál tábla, etc. Más mian leat aon cheann de na roghanna seo a "
"úsáid, imirce a chruthú le :class:'~django.db.migrations.operations.RunSQL' "
"oibríocht ina bhfuil ráitis ''ALTER TABLE'' a dhéanann an méid is mian leat "
"a dhéanamh."

msgid ""
"For example, if you're using MySQL and want your tables to use the MyISAM "
"table type, use the following SQL:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má tá MySQL á úsáid agat agus más mian leat do tháblaí an "
"cineál tábla MyISAM a úsáid, bain úsáid as an SQL seo a leanas:"

msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr "Fabhtcheartú"

msgid ""
"This page contains some advice about errors and problems commonly "
"encountered during the development of Django applications."
msgstr ""
"Tá roinnt comhairle ar an leathanach seo faoi earráidí agus fadhbanna a "
"bhíonn coitianta le linn iarratais Django a fhorbairt."

msgid "Problems running ``django-admin``"
msgstr "Fadhbanna ag rith ''django-admin''"

msgid "``command not found: django-admin``"
msgstr "''Ordú gan aimsiú: django-admin''"

msgid ""
":doc:`django-admin </ref/django-admin>` should be on your system path if you "
"installed Django via ``pip``. If it's not in your path, ensure you have your "
"virtual environment activated and you can try running the equivalent command "
"``python -m django``."
msgstr ""
":d oc:Ba chóir go mbeadh 'django-admin </ref/django-admin>' ar chosán an "
"chórais má shuiteáil tú Django trí ''pip''. Mura bhfuil sé i do chosán, "
"cinntigh go bhfuil do thimpeallacht fhíorúil gníomhachtaithe agat agus is "
"féidir leat triail a bhaint as an ordú coibhéiseach ''python -m django'' a "
"rith."

msgid "macOS permissions"
msgstr "ceadanna macOS"

msgid ""
"If you're using macOS, you may see the message \"permission denied\" when "
"you try to run ``django-admin``. This is because, on Unix-based systems like "
"macOS, a file must be marked as \"executable\" before it can be run as a "
"program. To do this, open Terminal.app and navigate (using the ``cd`` "
"command) to the directory where :doc:`django-admin </ref/django-admin>` is "
"installed, then run the command ``sudo chmod +x django-admin``."
msgstr ""
"Má tá macOS á úsáid agat, b'fhéidir go bhfeicfidh tú an teachtaireacht "
"\"cead diúltaithe\" nuair a dhéanann tú iarracht ''django-admin' a rith. Tá "
"sé seo toisc, ar chórais unix-bhunaithe cosúil le macOS, ní mór comhad a "
"mharcáil mar \"inrite\" sular féidir é a reáchtáil mar chlár. Chun seo a "
"dhéanamh, oscail Terminal.app agus nascleanúint (ag baint úsáide as an ordú "
"''cd''') chuig an eolaire ina bhfuil :d oc:'django-admin </ref/django-"
"admin>' suiteáilte, ansin rith an t-ordú ''sudo chmod +x django-admin''."

msgid "Miscellaneous"
msgstr "Ilghnéitheach"

msgid "I'm getting a ``UnicodeDecodeError``. What am I doing wrong?"
msgstr ""
"Tá ''UnicodeDecodeError' á fháil agam. Cad atá á dhéanamh agam mícheart?"

msgid ""
"This class of errors happen when a bytestring containing non-ASCII sequences "
"is transformed into a Unicode string and the specified encoding is "
"incorrect. The output generally looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"Tarlaíonn an aicme earráidí seo nuair a dhéantar foshraith ina bhfuil "
"seichimh neamh-ASCII a chlaochlú ina teaghrán Unicode agus nuair a bhíonn an "
"t-ionchódú sonraithe mícheart. Breathnaíonn an t-aschur go ginearálta mar "
"seo:"

msgid ""
"The resolution mostly depends on the context, however here are two common "
"pitfalls producing this error:"
msgstr ""
"Braitheann an rún den chuid is mó ar an gcomhthéacs, ach anseo tá dhá "
"pitfalls coitianta a tháirgeann an earráid seo:"

msgid ""
"Your system locale may be a default ASCII locale, like the \"C\" locale on "
"UNIX-like systems (can be checked by the ``locale`` command). If it's the "
"case, please refer to your system documentation to learn how you can change "
"this to a UTF-8 locale."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh logán do chórais a bheith ina logán réamhshocraithe ASCII, "
"cosúil leis an logán \"C\" ar chórais cosúil le UNIX (is féidir leis an ordú "
"''locale'' é a sheiceáil). Más amhlaidh atá, féach ar dhoiciméadú do chórais "
"chun a fháil amach conas is féidir leat é seo a athrú go logán UTF-8."

msgid "Related resources:"
msgstr "Acmhainní gaolmhara:"

msgid ":doc:`Unicode in Django </ref/unicode>`"
msgstr ":d oc:'Unicode in Django </ref/unicode>'"

msgid "https://wiki.python.org/moin/UnicodeDecodeError"
msgstr "https://wiki.python.org/moin/UnicodeDecodeError"

msgid "FAQ: Using Django"
msgstr "Ceisteanna Coitianta: Ag baint úsáide as Django"

msgid "Why do I get an error about importing :envvar:`DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE`?"
msgstr ""
"Cén fáth a bhfaighidh mé earráid faoi "
"iompórtáil:envvar:'DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE'?"

msgid "Make sure that:"
msgstr "Cinntigh an méid seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"The environment variable :envvar:`DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` is set to a fully-"
"qualified Python module (i.e. ``mysite.settings``)."
msgstr ""
"Tá an athróg timpeallachta :envvar:'DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE' socraithe do "
"mhodúl Python láncháilithe (i.e. ''mysite.settings'')."

msgid ""
"Said module is on ``sys.path`` (``import mysite.settings`` should work)."
msgstr ""
"Tá an modúl sin ar ''sys.path'' ('import mysite.settings'' ba chóir go n-"
"oibreodh sé)."

msgid "The module doesn't contain syntax errors."
msgstr "Níl earráidí comhréire sa mhodúl."

msgid "I can't stand your template language. Do I have to use it?"
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir liom do theanga teimpléid a sheasamh. An gcaithfidh mé é a úsáid?"

msgid ""
"We happen to think our template engine is the best thing since chunky bacon, "
"but we recognize that choosing a template language runs close to religion. "
"There's nothing about Django that requires using the template language, so "
"if you're attached to Jinja2, Mako, or whatever, feel free to use those."
msgstr ""
"Tarlaíonn sé go gceapann muid gurb é ár n-inneall teimpléad an rud is fearr "
"ó bhagún smutánach, ach aithnímid go ritheann roghnú teanga teimpléid gar do "
"reiligiún. Níl aon rud faoi Django a éilíonn úsáid a bhaint as an teanga "
"teimpléad, mar sin má tá tú ceangailte le Jinja2, Mako, nó cibé rud, bíodh "
"leisce ort iad sin a úsáid."

msgid "Do I have to use your model/database layer?"
msgstr "An gcaithfidh mé do shraith mhúnla / bunachar sonraí a úsáid?"

msgid ""
"Nope. Just like the template system, the model/database layer is decoupled "
"from the rest of the framework."
msgstr ""
"Nope. Díreach cosúil leis an gcóras teimpléid, tá an ciseal samhail / "
"bunachar sonraí díchúpláilte ón gcuid eile den chreat."

msgid ""
"The one exception is: If you use a different database library, you won't get "
"to use Django's automatically-generated admin site. That app is coupled to "
"the Django database layer."
msgstr ""
"Is é an eisceacht amháin: Má úsáideann tú leabharlann bunachar sonraí "
"difriúil, ní bhfaighidh tú suíomh riaracháin Django a ghintear go "
"huathoibríoch a úsáid. Tá an aip sin ceangailte le ciseal bunachar sonraí "
"Django."

msgid "How do I use image and file fields?"
msgstr "Conas a úsáidim réimsí íomhá agus comhaid?"

msgid ""
"Using a :class:`~django.db.models.FileField` or "
"an :class:`~django.db.models.ImageField` in a model takes a few steps:"
msgstr ""
"Ag baint úsáide as :class:'~django.db.models.FileField' "
"nó :class:'~django.db.models.ImageField' i múnla Bíonn cúpla céim:"

msgid ""
"In your settings file, you'll need to define :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT` as the "
"full path to a directory where you'd like Django to store uploaded files. "
"(For performance, these files are not stored in the database.) "
"Define :setting:`MEDIA_URL` as the base public URL of that directory. Make "
"sure that this directory is writable by the web server's user account."
msgstr ""
"I do chomhad socruithe, beidh ort :setting:'MEDIA_ROOT' a shainmhíniú mar an "
"cosán iomlán chuig eolaire inar mhaith leat Django chun comhaid uaslódáilte "
"a stóráil. (Le haghaidh feidhmíochta, ní stóráiltear na comhaid seo sa "
"bhunachar sonraí.) Sainmhínigh :setting:'MEDIA_URL' mar bhun-URL poiblí an "
"eolaire sin. Cinntigh go bhfuil an chomhadlann seo inscríofa ag cuntas "
"úsáideora an fhreastalaí gréasáin."

msgid ""
"Add the :class:`~django.db.models.FileField` "
"or :class:`~django.db.models.ImageField` to your model, defining "
"the :attr:`~django.db.models.FileField.upload_to` option to specify a "
"subdirectory of :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT` to use for uploaded files."
msgstr ""
"Cuir an :class:'~django.db.models.FileField' "
"nó :class:'~django.db.models.ImageField' le do mhúnla, ag sainiú an "
"rogha :attr:'~django.db.models.FileField.upload_to' chun fochomhadlann "
"de :setting:'MEDIA_ROOT' a shonrú le húsáid le haghaidh comhaid uaslódáilte."

msgid ""
"All that will be stored in your database is a path to the file (relative "
"to :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT`). You'll most likely want to use the "
"convenience :attr:`~django.db.models.fields.files.FieldFile.url` attribute "
"provided by Django. For example, if "
"your :class:`~django.db.models.ImageField` is called ``mug_shot``, you can "
"get the absolute path to your image in a template with "
"``{{ object.mug_shot.url }}``."
msgstr ""
"Is cosán chuig an gcomhad é gach rud a stórálfar i do bhunachar sonraí (i "
"gcoibhneas le :setting:'MEDIA_ROOT'). Is dócha gur mhaith leat an áisiúlacht "
"a úsáid:attr:'~django.db.models.fields.files.FieldFile.url' tréith a "
"sholáthraíonn Django. Mar shampla, má thugtar ''mug_shot' ar "
"do :class:'~django.db.models.ImageField', is féidir leat an cosán iomlán a "
"fháil ar d'íomhá i dteimpléad le ''{{ object.mug_shot.url }}''."

msgid "How do I make a variable available to all my templates?"
msgstr "Conas is féidir liom athróg a chur ar fáil do mo theimpléid go léir?"

msgid ""
"Sometimes your templates all need the same thing. A common example would be "
"dynamically generated menus. At first glance, it seems logical to add a "
"common dictionary to the template context."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta bíonn an rud céanna de dhíth ar do theimpléid. Sampla coitianta a "
"bheadh ann ná biachláir a ghintear go dinimiciúil. Ar an gcéad amharc, is "
"cosúil go bhfuil sé loighciúil foclóir coiteann a chur le comhthéacs an "
"teimpléid."

msgid ""
"The best way to do this in Django is to use a ``RequestContext``. Details on "
"how to do this are here: :ref:`subclassing-context-requestcontext`."
msgstr ""
"Is é an bealach is fearr chun é seo a dhéanamh in Django ná "
"''RequestContext' a úsáid. Tá sonraí maidir le conas é seo a dhéanamh "
"anseo: :ref:'subclassing-context-requestcontext'."
